WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:56.057
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:56.327 --> 01:03.293
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
01:05.003 --> 01:07.088
EPISODE 1

4
01:49.672 --> 01:52.383
SPRING 1932, GYEONGSEONG

5
01:52.884 --> 01:54.260
Rickshaw coming through!

6
02:12.237 --> 02:13.238
Damn it.

7
02:17.575 --> 02:19.994
Something good better be coming my way today.

8
02:22.413 --> 02:23.831
-Out of the way. -Move.

9
02:23.915 --> 02:25.375
-Out of the way. -Extra!

10
02:48.022 --> 02:51.484
This stop is Keijo, Keijo Station.

11
02:52.193 --> 02:55.488
Please ensure you have all your belongings before you get off.

12
02:56.322 --> 02:59.867
Thank you for using our service today.

13
03:24.517 --> 03:25.768
I'll get your bag down.

14
03:26.936 --> 03:28.271
It's okay.

15
03:28.354 --> 03:29.647
I'll do it.

16
03:51.502 --> 03:52.420
So-ran!

17
04:33.086 --> 04:35.338
Does he not watch where he's going?

18
04:35.421 --> 04:36.839
Thank you.

19
04:41.052 --> 04:42.929
-Excuse me. -Yes?

20
04:43.012 --> 04:46.099
This is Changgyeongwon, right?

21
04:46.182 --> 04:48.017
Well, Changgyeongwon is…

22
04:48.101 --> 04:51.270
Go straight to the left, then turn right.

23
04:52.105 --> 04:53.314
-Thank you. -My pleasure.

24
05:06.369 --> 05:07.578
Thank you.

25
05:08.704 --> 05:10.665
You have something here.

26
05:13.584 --> 05:14.836
Thank you.

27
05:33.104 --> 05:35.440
Thank you. It slipped out of my hand.

28
06:13.644 --> 06:15.605
Who's here? What's all this about?

29
06:16.731 --> 06:19.859
It's the inspector general of the Government-General of Joseon.

30
06:20.943 --> 06:22.278
The inspector general…

31
06:23.112 --> 06:24.322
Is he someone important?

32
06:25.031 --> 06:26.199
Look, miss.

33
06:26.282 --> 06:31.746
The inspector general is the Government-General's number two.

34
06:32.872 --> 06:35.208
You don't even know what an inspector general is.

35
06:35.291 --> 06:38.336
How could you know what "number two" means?

36
06:38.419 --> 06:39.629
Of course I do.

37
06:39.712 --> 06:42.465
It means he's second only to the Governor-General.

38
06:42.548 --> 06:44.550
Well, well. How do you understand English?

39
06:44.634 --> 06:46.052
And you're a woman at that.

40
06:47.386 --> 06:49.138
I speak a little English myself.

41
06:49.222 --> 06:50.181
Yeah, sure.

42
07:11.160 --> 07:12.203
Thank you.

43
07:15.915 --> 07:18.793
Welcome to Joseon, Inspector General.

44
07:18.876 --> 07:20.962
Thank you, Interpreter Suzuki.

45
07:21.045 --> 07:22.755
-Have you been well? -Yes, sir.

46
07:22.838 --> 07:27.093
You look about ten years younger than you did in Tokyo last month.

47
07:27.176 --> 07:29.971
They say Keijo is quite a place. Seems the rumors are true.

48
07:30.513 --> 07:33.307
It's improved quite a bit since you were last here.

49
07:34.934 --> 07:35.977
That's good to hear.

50
07:38.479 --> 07:39.313
Fukuda!

51
07:40.898 --> 07:41.816
No,

52
07:41.899 --> 07:45.027
I should call you Chief of Police of the Government-General of Joseon now.

53
07:45.945 --> 07:47.154
Has it been ten years?

54
07:48.030 --> 07:49.073
Yes, sir.

55
07:49.156 --> 07:51.325
It's an honor to serve you again.

56
07:54.036 --> 07:54.912
This is…

57
08:02.753 --> 08:03.629
Who is that?

58
08:04.505 --> 08:09.218
He's a WWP News Keijo correspondent, the one I mentioned in Tokyo.

59
08:10.344 --> 08:11.679
I see.

60
08:11.762 --> 08:13.598
You said he's Joseon-American?

61
08:13.681 --> 08:18.603
Yes, he's from Hawaii. He was based in Shanghai, China until three months ago.

62
08:18.686 --> 08:21.022
He's quite friendly toward our Government-General.

63
08:22.440 --> 08:25.109
Then have him come over. I should introduce myself.

64
08:25.192 --> 08:28.279
He's an American reporter. With what's happening in Manchukuo,

65
08:28.362 --> 08:31.240
he's someone our home country would keep a close eye on.

66
08:32.908 --> 08:34.160
We should keep him on our side.

67
08:34.744 --> 08:35.661
Yes, sir.

68
08:36.495 --> 08:37.747
Mr. Yoo Philip!

69
08:40.583 --> 08:41.667
One moment.

70
08:54.764 --> 08:56.515
A Chinese couple?

71
08:58.809 --> 08:59.769
Nice to meet you.

72
08:59.852 --> 09:03.689
I'm Yoo Philip, Keijo correspondent for the American WWP News Agency.

73
09:03.773 --> 09:05.900
It's a great honor to meet you.

74
09:05.983 --> 09:07.276
No, the honor is mine.

75
09:07.360 --> 09:11.364
Nothing's scarier than a journalist's pen these days.

76
09:11.447 --> 09:13.824
I hope you'll be gentle with us.

77
09:17.244 --> 09:18.162
Please don't worry.

78
09:21.874 --> 09:25.086
Allow me to introduce my wife. She's Chinese.

79
09:26.379 --> 09:29.674
I first came to Keijo three months ago,

80
09:29.757 --> 09:32.259
and she arrived from Shanghai just now.

81
09:33.552 --> 09:35.304
My congratulations on your reunion.

82
09:36.681 --> 09:38.432
And congratulations on the little one.

83
09:39.517 --> 09:42.144
Thank you. My wife cannot speak Japanese.

84
09:44.397 --> 09:46.899
He kindly congratulated us on our baby on the way.

85
09:49.151 --> 09:50.194
Thank you.

86
09:50.778 --> 09:51.987
You speak the Joseon language.

87
09:53.030 --> 09:56.033
Now that you're in Gyeongseong, you should learn Japanese.

88
09:56.742 --> 09:59.078
Sir, I must say you speak the language so well.

89
10:00.413 --> 10:01.956
Does it sound okay?

90
10:02.039 --> 10:04.875
I left Joseon more than ten years ago, so I've forgotten quite a lot.

91
10:04.959 --> 10:06.585
You still speak it better than I do.

92
10:09.588 --> 10:11.924
Let's get together for a meal sometime soon.

93
10:12.007 --> 10:14.176
Yes, I was actually hoping to have you over.

94
10:14.260 --> 10:16.220
How about at our place?

95
10:16.971 --> 10:18.180
Would that be all right?

96
10:18.264 --> 10:19.306
We would be honored.

97
10:19.390 --> 10:22.935
How about next Thursday?

98
10:23.018 --> 10:24.061
Very well.

99
10:24.145 --> 10:26.313
All right, we'll talk more then.

100
10:27.314 --> 10:28.441
Is Hideo not here yet?

101
10:29.775 --> 10:31.318
My son and daughter came with me.

102
10:34.739 --> 10:36.615
Is that a chair with wheels?

103
10:38.033 --> 10:39.452
Please, no pushing.

104
10:41.954 --> 10:43.122
Excuse me.

105
10:43.205 --> 10:44.874
I didn't know you had a daughter.

106
10:44.957 --> 10:46.709
I have a 12-year-old girl.

107
10:46.792 --> 10:49.336
She's excited. It's her first time in Gyeongseong.

108
10:49.420 --> 10:50.588
That's natural at her age.

109
10:53.507 --> 10:54.967
-What's the matter? -My bag…

110
11:00.973 --> 11:02.391
What's wrong?

111
11:19.742 --> 11:21.494
We'll be conducting a brief inspection.

112
11:21.577 --> 11:23.037
Form a single line, everyone!

113
11:23.120 --> 11:24.955
What's going on? Is it a pickpocket?

114
11:31.712 --> 11:32.838
I think it's that way.

115
11:39.637 --> 11:40.679
A bag was stolen?

116
11:42.306 --> 11:44.809
Did someone steal a bag in this crowd?

117
11:57.613 --> 12:01.200
I left something in my seat, but this isn't where I was sitting.

118
12:12.253 --> 12:13.128
Oh my.

119
12:13.212 --> 12:14.797
Babe, what was your name?

120
12:14.880 --> 12:15.714
What?

121
12:15.798 --> 12:17.716
Never mind. "Gorgeous" will do.

122
12:18.467 --> 12:20.094
-Oh dear. Excuse us. -Excuse me.

123
12:27.893 --> 12:29.436
FIRST-CLASS COMPARTMENT

124
12:40.948 --> 12:42.491
-I'm sorry. -I'm sorry.

125
12:43.659 --> 12:45.119
-I'm sorry. -I'm sorry.

126
12:48.414 --> 12:49.707
Are you from Joseon?

127
12:55.170 --> 12:57.840
Sorry, I just assumed because you spoke the language.

128
12:57.923 --> 12:59.508
I'm also from mainland Japan.

129
13:03.762 --> 13:04.638
One second.

130
13:09.685 --> 13:10.978
Thank you.

131
13:19.904 --> 13:20.988
Come on, let's go.

132
13:22.948 --> 13:23.991
Please go ahead.

133
13:24.074 --> 13:26.535
Go this way. That way is closed off.

134
13:28.203 --> 13:29.079
Well then.

135
13:29.747 --> 13:33.292
No, you can't go through that door.

136
13:35.002 --> 13:37.254
I said you can't go that way.

137
13:37.338 --> 13:38.213
Wait…

138
13:59.652 --> 14:00.694
Excuse me.

139
14:02.112 --> 14:04.281
Yes? Me?

140
14:05.115 --> 14:07.493
Haven't you seen a picture of the princess in the newspaper?

141
14:08.661 --> 14:09.536
Sorry?

142
14:10.537 --> 14:13.123
Look at all the crowd waiting to welcome her.

143
14:14.541 --> 14:17.920
Doesn't it occur to you that she might actually be the princess?

144
14:24.259 --> 14:25.511
I'm sorry.

145
14:25.594 --> 14:26.428
I'm sorry.

146
14:26.512 --> 14:28.138
Though of course she isn't.

147
14:30.557 --> 14:31.558
Well then.

148
14:32.810 --> 14:34.311
Hey, hold on.

149
14:42.528 --> 14:44.446
I really thought she was the princess.

150
14:51.745 --> 14:53.747
FIRST CLASS

151
15:19.565 --> 15:20.482
Thank you.

152
15:29.366 --> 15:30.743
A bag was stolen?

153
15:31.368 --> 15:34.079
Yes, so you can exchange greetings later.

154
15:34.163 --> 15:35.164
It's cold.

155
15:36.790 --> 15:37.666
Are you cold?

156
15:37.750 --> 15:38.959
Hold on, Hanako.

157
15:52.639 --> 15:55.392
No, you can't go through that door.

158
15:57.311 --> 15:59.688
Where are you going?

159
15:59.772 --> 16:01.648
Hold on, Hanako.

160
16:01.732 --> 16:03.525
I said I'm cold.

161
16:09.823 --> 16:10.699
I'm sorry.

162
16:10.783 --> 16:13.952
Is it always winter in Joseon?

163
16:14.036 --> 16:16.747
It's March, but it's still too cold.

164
16:18.082 --> 16:18.916
No.

165
16:22.002 --> 16:24.797
Spring will soon be here in Joseon too.

166
16:28.675 --> 16:31.929
Could I speak with the police?

167
16:33.764 --> 16:36.016
Why don't you take a taxi?

168
16:36.100 --> 16:37.726
How about a tour of Gyeongseong?

169
16:37.810 --> 16:41.688
Joseon Shrine, Gyeongseong Shrine, Jangchungdan Shrine, then turn, okay?

170
16:41.772 --> 16:42.815
Do you go to America too?

171
16:42.898 --> 16:44.942
What? America?

172
16:45.025 --> 16:46.610
Welcome!

173
16:47.319 --> 16:48.779
I'm going to America.

174
16:48.862 --> 16:51.865
Sure, ma'am, I'll take you there.

175
16:55.452 --> 16:56.662
Here we go.

176
17:00.749 --> 17:04.419
You were taking so long. I thought you went to America without telling me.

177
17:04.503 --> 17:06.463
In spirit, I'm already there.

178
17:23.230 --> 17:28.402
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

179
17:50.174 --> 17:51.216
APPRAISAL

180
17:53.135 --> 17:54.011
Damn it.

181
17:58.223 --> 17:59.141
Hey.

182
18:01.768 --> 18:02.728
Goodbye.

183
18:03.687 --> 18:06.315
JONGNO PAWNSHOP

184
18:08.233 --> 18:09.359
Come on.

185
18:17.743 --> 18:19.870
Hey, did you see who arrived at the station?

186
18:19.953 --> 18:21.914
He's the Government-General's number two.

187
18:21.997 --> 18:23.332
Number two?

188
18:23.415 --> 18:24.625
What, English again?

189
18:27.753 --> 18:31.006
If I'd grown up in a missionary's house like you did,

190
18:31.089 --> 18:32.424
I'd have learned English too.

191
18:33.050 --> 18:35.552
Do you think being a live-in maid was easy?

192
18:36.303 --> 18:38.180
Of course I know it was hard.

193
18:38.263 --> 18:41.600
When I first met you, you were crying outside that house.

194
18:41.683 --> 18:44.895
You were accused of stealing food and got beaten for it.

195
18:45.520 --> 18:46.647
And the next day,

196
18:46.730 --> 18:49.566
the missionary felt bad and gave you rice, didn't he?

197
18:49.650 --> 18:52.819
Right. But they weren't mistaken.

198
18:52.903 --> 18:54.196
Wait, what?

199
18:54.696 --> 18:57.866
I really did steal their bread.

200
18:58.700 --> 19:00.577
What? You actually did?

201
19:00.661 --> 19:03.038
Yes, I was starving.

202
19:03.121 --> 19:05.332
I shed a few tears, and they all fell for it.

203
19:05.415 --> 19:08.418
Hey, how could you not have told me that all this time?

204
19:08.502 --> 19:10.629
You never asked, dummy.

205
19:10.712 --> 19:12.506
Would you have told me if I'd asked?

206
19:13.048 --> 19:13.966
Answer me.

207
19:19.763 --> 19:21.890
Hey, Lee Ga-kyung!

208
19:33.944 --> 19:35.153
You were taking forever.

209
19:36.488 --> 19:38.282
I thought you'd run off again.

210
19:45.205 --> 19:46.999
Take it all out.

211
19:47.082 --> 19:49.584
If I catch you swiping anything again, you're dead.

212
19:50.252 --> 19:52.462
Cigarettes. Look at you.

213
19:52.546 --> 19:53.380
Go eat.

214
19:56.633 --> 19:58.719
Why'd you bring pine cones?

215
19:58.802 --> 20:01.096
You idiot. All you brought is junk.

216
20:01.722 --> 20:03.724
What do I do with you?

217
20:06.393 --> 20:07.394
Damn it.

218
20:07.477 --> 20:08.562
Go on, eat.

219
20:09.980 --> 20:11.064
One jeon?

220
20:11.857 --> 20:12.733
Work hard!

221
20:13.317 --> 20:14.651
-Yes, sir. -Now eat.

222
20:17.362 --> 20:18.363
Is this it?

223
20:18.947 --> 20:20.991
If anything turns up in your pockets,

224
20:21.074 --> 20:22.284
I'll beat you for every jeon.

225
20:25.495 --> 20:28.915
You little bastard, how dare you try to sneak some off?

226
20:28.999 --> 20:29.875
Eat up, asshole.

227
20:32.127 --> 20:33.462
Why are you empty-handed?

228
20:34.046 --> 20:37.049
You went to Itsukoshi Department Store. How come you've got nothing?

229
20:37.674 --> 20:40.719
Today, there were three policemen…

230
20:40.802 --> 20:43.138
What? Did you just say "policemen"?

231
20:44.473 --> 20:45.349
Hey!

232
20:46.600 --> 20:47.934
What are the police?

233
20:48.018 --> 20:50.562
The police are Boss's tomodachi.

234
20:51.355 --> 20:52.356
Did you hear that?

235
20:52.439 --> 20:54.941
The police are my friends.

236
20:55.567 --> 20:57.944
So that's no excuse.

237
20:58.028 --> 20:59.279
You little bastard.

238
21:00.155 --> 21:02.032
You get nothing to eat today.

239
21:06.828 --> 21:09.539
What are you, some kind of animal?

240
21:09.623 --> 21:11.625
That's disgusting.

241
21:14.086 --> 21:15.337
You got nothing either?

242
21:16.463 --> 21:17.756
Of course not.

243
21:25.722 --> 21:26.890
What is this crap?

244
21:36.233 --> 21:37.401
Here you go.

245
21:38.568 --> 21:39.653
Thank you.

246
21:40.737 --> 21:44.366
All of this together isn't even worth one won.

247
21:45.117 --> 21:47.953
After I bribe the police at Gyeongseong Station,

248
21:48.036 --> 21:49.413
what's left for me?

249
21:50.914 --> 21:54.376
You stole my money three years ago and ran off to sneak onto a ship.

250
21:54.459 --> 21:58.088
And when you were caught at Incheon Port, what did you promise me?

251
21:59.214 --> 22:01.258
If you fail to repay one won a day,

252
22:02.843 --> 22:04.845
or if I catch you sneaking something away…

253
22:08.682 --> 22:09.933
how were you going to repay me?

254
22:11.518 --> 22:13.061
Come on, Boss.

255
22:13.145 --> 22:15.564
You know Ga-kyung. That's not all she's got.

256
22:15.647 --> 22:16.940
Hold on.

257
22:17.607 --> 22:18.567
Here's the big one.

258
22:20.861 --> 22:22.237
You little bastard.

259
22:22.320 --> 22:23.989
You tried to sneak this away, huh?

260
22:24.072 --> 22:26.283
No, I was about to give it to you,

261
22:26.366 --> 22:28.910
but you were being so impatient.

262
22:28.994 --> 22:31.329
First, let go of this.

263
22:31.413 --> 22:34.958
If she hurts her wrist and can't work, who will lose out?

264
22:35.041 --> 22:36.084
Isn't that right?

265
22:36.168 --> 22:37.794
Stay out of this!

266
22:45.135 --> 22:46.344
Don't forget…

267
22:49.681 --> 22:50.849
what you promised me.

268
22:54.060 --> 22:54.895
Okay?

269
22:55.479 --> 22:56.354
Okay.

270
22:58.607 --> 23:02.277
-Neener-neener, neener-neener -Neener-neener, neener-neener

271
23:02.360 --> 23:06.448
-Neener-neener, neener-neener -Neener-neener, neener-neener

272
23:06.531 --> 23:10.368
-Kkot-nim can't walk -Kkot-nim can't walk

273
23:10.452 --> 23:12.078
-She can't walk -She can't walk

274
23:12.162 --> 23:14.498
I'll tell my sister and brother on you all!

275
23:14.581 --> 23:16.541
-Go on, tell 'em, Jap! -Go on, tell 'em, Jap!

276
23:16.625 --> 23:18.752
-Go to Japan and rot -Go to Japan and rot

277
23:18.835 --> 23:20.670
Damn it, I'm not Japanese!

278
23:20.754 --> 23:22.255
Hey, you brats!

279
23:23.048 --> 23:24.090
Get over here.

280
23:25.050 --> 23:26.259
You're at it again.

281
23:26.843 --> 23:28.220
Get over here! You little punks.

282
23:28.845 --> 23:31.765
You try picking on Kkot-nim again, I'll teach you a lesson!

283
23:31.848 --> 23:33.683
Kkot-nim, did they pick on you again?

284
23:33.767 --> 23:35.810
I know where you live!

285
23:37.562 --> 23:41.233
Kkot-nim, it's a big secret, so I've kept it from you all this time.

286
23:41.316 --> 23:42.609
But I think it's time you knew.

287
23:44.611 --> 23:45.487
Listen carefully.

288
23:46.279 --> 23:48.490
Kkot-nim, your mom and dad

289
23:48.573 --> 23:50.534
joined Ahn Jung-geun, the patriotic martyr,

290
23:50.617 --> 23:53.411
in assassinating Ito Hirobumi and died.

291
23:54.204 --> 23:57.582
They carried you on their backs, but then you were injured and could no longer walk.

292
23:57.666 --> 23:59.209
Wow, for real?

293
23:59.292 --> 24:02.087
Yeah. So next time they make fun of you--

294
24:03.755 --> 24:04.965
S…

295
24:05.549 --> 24:06.758
-S… what? -S… what?

296
24:07.926 --> 24:09.678
Kkot-nim, hold on.

297
24:11.304 --> 24:14.641
Lee No-ma. If you're going to lie, get your story straight.

298
24:15.433 --> 24:16.768
What's wrong with my story?

299
24:16.851 --> 24:20.355
Ahn Jung-geun assassinated Ito Hirobumi more than 20 years ago.

300
24:20.438 --> 24:22.023
If her parents died back then,

301
24:22.107 --> 24:23.525
how could she be 7 now?

302
24:25.527 --> 24:26.486
You're right.

303
24:27.070 --> 24:29.197
If you're going to lie, make it convincing.

304
24:29.281 --> 24:30.865
Otherwise, don't even bother.

305
24:31.825 --> 24:33.910
Even so, how could we possibly tell her…

306
24:34.869 --> 24:37.205
that her parents caught the disease from her and died,

307
24:37.289 --> 24:38.957
and that she's paralyzed for life?

308
24:39.708 --> 24:42.127
If we tell her that her parents

309
24:42.210 --> 24:45.046
gave their lives for independence,

310
24:45.755 --> 24:47.173
she can live with pride like I do.

311
24:47.257 --> 24:50.051
Pride? What does that even matter?

312
24:53.263 --> 24:54.139
Kkot-nim.

313
24:54.222 --> 24:57.309
Don't go telling people about the independence movement.

314
24:57.392 --> 25:00.854
No, just forget about it altogether.

315
25:00.937 --> 25:04.190
You want to eat millet porridge here or eat rice in an ondol house?

316
25:04.274 --> 25:05.817
I want rice.

317
25:05.900 --> 25:06.818
Right?

318
25:06.901 --> 25:10.113
So you should just think about living a good life.

319
25:10.196 --> 25:11.656
Got it?

320
25:14.284 --> 25:15.410
Hey, Lee Ga-kyung.

321
25:15.493 --> 25:19.080
What devilish nonsense are you rattling on about?

322
25:19.164 --> 25:20.874
The independence movement means nothing?

323
25:20.957 --> 25:21.958
Are you not one of us?

324
25:22.042 --> 25:23.418
Why does that matter?

325
25:23.501 --> 25:27.631
Let's be frank. What did your parents dying for independence in 1919 get you?

326
25:29.090 --> 25:30.550
It didn't bring independence.

327
25:30.634 --> 25:32.719
It just left you orphaned and suffering.

328
25:32.802 --> 25:33.637
Do you like that?

329
25:33.720 --> 25:36.973
Still, I'm proud of my parents for fighting for independence.

330
25:37.057 --> 25:38.892
I don't envy those who sold out our country

331
25:38.975 --> 25:40.935
or the Japs who live comfortably at all.

332
25:41.519 --> 25:43.313
If I'd been 10 in 1919,

333
25:43.396 --> 25:45.357
I'd have been out there shouting for independence.

334
25:45.440 --> 25:48.276
Yeah, right. Whatever.

335
25:48.360 --> 25:50.820
Then why aren't you fighting for independence now?

336
25:50.904 --> 25:52.947
Why take Japanese passengers in your rickshaw?

337
25:53.657 --> 25:54.658
Yeah, why?

338
25:57.077 --> 25:59.079
-That's different. -Whatever.

339
25:59.162 --> 26:01.081
The independence movement is none of my concern.

340
26:01.164 --> 26:03.166
I'll save up so I can leave this country.

341
26:03.249 --> 26:04.334
I'm going to America.

342
26:06.878 --> 26:07.754
America?

343
26:07.837 --> 26:09.839
There she goes again with America.

344
26:25.397 --> 26:26.815
-Watch your step. -All right.

345
26:40.912 --> 26:41.746
The bag…

346
26:43.164 --> 26:43.998
What do we do?

347
26:44.916 --> 26:48.128
Even if the thief finds what's in there,

348
26:48.211 --> 26:50.839
we can only hope nothing goes wrong until after next Thursday.

349
27:12.402 --> 27:14.320
This is the living room.

350
27:20.118 --> 27:21.161
And this is…

351
27:24.038 --> 27:25.081
the dining room.

352
27:33.506 --> 27:36.259
And the kitchen is further inside.

353
27:36.968 --> 27:38.052
The bathroom is here.

354
27:41.055 --> 27:43.433
And this is my room.

355
27:48.438 --> 27:51.983
Upstairs, there's a living room, a study, and a larger bedroom.

356
28:09.584 --> 28:11.169
You can use this room.

357
28:12.378 --> 28:13.213
All right, then.

358
28:16.549 --> 28:17.801
Let's share this room.

359
28:21.346 --> 28:22.180
Pardon?

360
28:23.431 --> 28:24.599
We're a married couple.

361
28:25.350 --> 28:29.020
Someone might drop by. We'd look more natural sharing a room.

362
28:29.687 --> 28:32.982
I'll keep wearing this belly wrap.

363
28:39.531 --> 28:41.658
Right. Understood.

364
28:57.549 --> 28:59.050
Someone stole your wallet?

365
29:00.343 --> 29:01.886
Yes, I'm sorry.

366
29:01.970 --> 29:04.347
Was there something important in it?

367
29:06.099 --> 29:06.975
Not really.

368
29:09.519 --> 29:12.146
Then don't waste your time over a little money.

369
29:14.691 --> 29:15.525
Yes, sir.

370
29:37.005 --> 29:38.298
Welcome.

371
29:39.048 --> 29:40.717
Have you been well, Yanagi?

372
29:53.396 --> 29:54.564
What are you all doing?

373
30:20.965 --> 30:21.799
Let's go.

374
30:26.971 --> 30:31.309
If I had a million won

375
30:31.851 --> 30:35.730
I'd buy a gold hairpin and a fancy ring

376
30:35.813 --> 30:38.942
And I'd even buy a plane

377
30:39.025 --> 30:40.735
And fly high above the clouds

378
30:40.818 --> 30:42.737
Spinning round and round

379
30:42.820 --> 30:46.908
No, stop dreaming of a million won

380
30:46.991 --> 30:51.371
Or you'll waste your youth Chasing a foolish dream

381
30:52.747 --> 30:53.831
There.

382
30:53.915 --> 30:55.458
Let's see what's in there.

383
30:55.541 --> 30:57.585
Come on, something big.

384
31:01.881 --> 31:02.799
Clothes.

385
31:03.925 --> 31:04.842
More clothes.

386
31:04.926 --> 31:07.345
I hid it away in case it was worth something.

387
31:07.428 --> 31:08.596
It's just clothes?

388
31:11.683 --> 31:12.809
My goodness.

389
31:13.434 --> 31:16.562
My, my. What could this be?

390
31:16.646 --> 31:18.231
It feels heavy.

391
31:19.857 --> 31:20.984
Let's see.

392
31:23.027 --> 31:24.445
What's with the rice?

393
31:24.529 --> 31:25.697
Wow, rice!

394
31:25.780 --> 31:27.407
I haven't seen white rice in years.

395
31:27.490 --> 31:28.658
I'm going to sell this.

396
31:28.741 --> 31:31.995
Kkot-nim, don't tell me you want to eat this, okay?

397
31:34.163 --> 31:35.999
The bag was disappointing,

398
31:36.082 --> 31:37.291
but I can tell this is it.

399
31:37.917 --> 31:40.211
I stepped in dog poop earlier.

400
31:40.294 --> 31:41.921
Dog poop, I'm counting on you.

401
31:42.005 --> 31:43.923
Yes. Come on, give us a jackpot.

402
31:47.051 --> 31:47.927
Meh? That's it?

403
31:48.594 --> 31:49.470
It's three won.

404
31:49.554 --> 31:52.223
Jeez, only three won from a first-class passenger?

405
31:54.308 --> 31:55.685
I need to poop.

406
31:55.768 --> 31:58.479
Hey, I asked for a big drop, not a big dump.

407
32:01.024 --> 32:01.858
Let's go.

408
32:03.943 --> 32:06.446
Right, you can keep all those clothes.

409
32:06.529 --> 32:08.781
I'll take 10% of that three won.

410
32:10.783 --> 32:12.076
That makes it…

411
32:12.160 --> 32:13.453
Yeah, three jeon.

412
32:14.620 --> 32:16.372
Hey, make sure I get my cut.

413
32:16.456 --> 32:17.290
Can you hold it?

414
32:20.126 --> 32:24.630
Hey, one won is 100 jeon, so ten percent of three won is 30 jeon.

415
32:26.007 --> 32:28.301
What would he do without me?

416
32:29.927 --> 32:33.097
"Tokyo Imperial University."

417
32:34.849 --> 32:35.975
"Literature…"

418
32:37.894 --> 32:39.145
"Department"?

419
32:39.228 --> 32:40.063
"Department."

420
32:41.064 --> 32:43.608
"English Literature."

421
32:46.778 --> 32:49.197
What's a Tokyo Imperial student doing in Gyeongseong?

422
32:50.406 --> 32:51.449
His name is…

423
32:58.331 --> 32:59.582
What?

424
32:59.665 --> 33:00.833
Isn't this a pawn ticket?

425
33:00.917 --> 33:02.919
"Jongno Pawnshop."

426
33:03.544 --> 33:05.713
"1919."

427
33:05.797 --> 33:07.256
"Sin Tae-jin."

428
33:10.093 --> 33:11.260
Not worth a thing.

429
33:15.723 --> 33:17.642
What a bust.

430
33:30.113 --> 33:31.280
What's wrong with this?

431
33:57.598 --> 33:58.474
A bullet?

432
33:59.392 --> 34:00.518
It's a bullet.

433
34:10.444 --> 34:12.405
I knew the dog poop wouldn't let me down.

434
34:15.616 --> 34:20.580
Three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine.

435
34:26.836 --> 34:30.548
I apologize for not being able to attend your wife's funeral last year.

436
34:30.631 --> 34:32.258
Don't worry about it.

437
34:32.341 --> 34:35.678
No need to come all the way from Keijo to Tokyo for something trivial.

438
34:41.392 --> 34:42.894
It's fruitcake.

439
34:42.977 --> 34:45.021
-Itsukoshi Department Store? -Yes, sir.

440
34:45.688 --> 34:49.025
Last time you were in Keijo, wasn't Itsukoshi a drapery shop?

441
34:49.192 --> 34:54.864
They built and opened a big Keijo branch on Bonjeong Avenue.

442
34:55.990 --> 34:58.784
The plaza in front of it became so clean.

443
35:00.786 --> 35:02.705
The old drapery shop

444
35:02.788 --> 35:05.875
used to be crawling with Josenjing pickpockets.

445
35:09.462 --> 35:10.296
I'm aware.

446
35:11.130 --> 35:12.965
I used to be one of them myself.

447
35:25.353 --> 35:26.520
My apologies.

448
35:27.438 --> 35:28.689
I didn't mean to offend you.

449
35:31.442 --> 35:32.526
It's quite all right.

450
35:33.653 --> 35:35.571
I'll take it as a compliment

451
35:35.655 --> 35:38.908
that Hideo has become such a fine Japanese citizen.

452
35:39.575 --> 35:40.409
Indeed.

453
35:41.035 --> 35:42.620
That's precisely what I meant.

454
35:43.663 --> 35:45.623
He's not just an ordinary citizen.

455
35:45.706 --> 35:48.876
He graduated from the Army Academy and Tokyo Imperial University.

456
35:48.960 --> 35:52.171
He's an interpreter trainee for the Government-General of Joseon,

457
35:52.255 --> 35:54.674
fluent in Japanese, English, and the Joseon language, no less.

458
35:56.842 --> 35:59.637
No one would think that Hideo is from Joseon.

459
36:01.347 --> 36:04.725
Hideo couldn't speak a word of Japanese when we first met.

460
36:04.809 --> 36:05.685
Do you remember?

461
36:18.656 --> 36:20.491
What do you think you're doing?

462
36:21.659 --> 36:22.827
What is it?

463
36:22.910 --> 36:24.078
Pickpocket!

464
36:25.037 --> 36:26.789
Police!

465
36:29.583 --> 36:31.294
Why won't you beg me to spare you?

466
36:32.503 --> 36:33.713
You don't know Japanese.

467
36:38.009 --> 36:39.802
Why won't you beg me to spare you?

468
36:40.803 --> 36:42.263
Whether I get caught and killed

469
36:43.431 --> 36:44.974
or starve to death on the street,

470
36:46.183 --> 36:47.351
it makes no difference.

471
36:50.313 --> 36:51.856
Hurry, over there.

472
36:53.774 --> 36:54.984
What a nuisance.

473
36:55.818 --> 36:57.111
Is this the pickpocket?

474
36:57.820 --> 36:59.155
Not this one.

475
37:11.417 --> 37:12.335
Watch closely.

476
37:13.794 --> 37:14.754
The pickpocket…

477
37:17.006 --> 37:17.882
A gun!

478
37:22.553 --> 37:23.471
…is that kid.

479
37:41.739 --> 37:44.033
Do you remember that day?

480
37:46.660 --> 37:47.536
I don't.

481
37:48.871 --> 37:51.332
It was too long ago. I don't remember.

482
38:25.866 --> 38:27.701
Can't you sleep?

483
38:31.122 --> 38:31.997
Shoot.

484
38:32.081 --> 38:32.915
No!

485
38:38.379 --> 38:40.631
I've waited 13 years.

486
38:43.175 --> 38:46.011
Yet waiting a few more days feels even harder.

487
39:04.905 --> 39:06.532
-Get out. -Auntie.

488
39:08.617 --> 39:09.577
Get out.

489
39:09.660 --> 39:11.245
You disgust me.

490
39:11.328 --> 39:12.705
That filthy blood!

491
39:12.788 --> 39:14.331
Get out of my house!

492
40:01.420 --> 40:02.588
Weren't you sleeping?

493
40:02.671 --> 40:03.506
No.

494
40:05.257 --> 40:06.258
Hey, you know what?

495
40:07.384 --> 40:08.677
I'm just wondering.

496
40:10.095 --> 40:13.349
If your money and I both fell into the water, which would you save?

497
40:13.432 --> 40:14.266
You.

498
40:16.727 --> 40:17.603
Really?

499
40:18.437 --> 40:19.522
Yeah.

500
40:19.605 --> 40:20.523
Seriously?

501
40:23.526 --> 40:24.652
Hold on.

502
40:28.989 --> 40:31.033
Oh, but I was lying!

503
40:31.116 --> 40:32.868
Why are you always messing with me?

504
40:35.538 --> 40:38.123
You learned that from the foreign missionary.

505
40:38.207 --> 40:40.084
You cross your fingers when you lie.

506
40:40.793 --> 40:42.086
What if you do this?

507
40:42.169 --> 40:44.255
It means "wish me luck."

508
40:45.130 --> 40:46.131
Right.

509
40:46.215 --> 40:50.469
How does that go from lying to wishing for good luck?

510
40:51.345 --> 40:55.599
It means you're wishing for luck so nobody catches you lying.

511
40:57.935 --> 41:00.020
I always cross my fingers every time I pickpocket,

512
41:00.104 --> 41:01.230
so I won't get caught.

513
41:02.231 --> 41:03.774
Maybe that's why you never get caught.

514
41:05.985 --> 41:07.111
By the way,

515
41:08.153 --> 41:10.781
when you save up enough money, will you really go to America?

516
41:12.074 --> 41:13.117
Yeah.

517
41:13.200 --> 41:15.703
I'm going to leave Joseon, no matter what.

518
41:17.997 --> 41:19.665
I'm sick and tired of this place.

519
41:20.583 --> 41:21.792
It's miserable here.

520
41:23.836 --> 41:24.712
Yeah.

521
41:25.296 --> 41:27.423
Anywhere should be better than this dump.

522
41:28.424 --> 41:29.758
But why America?

523
41:32.344 --> 41:34.305
Just because.

524
41:36.515 --> 41:37.683
Okay.

525
42:03.000 --> 42:04.418
-Forty. -Fifty.

526
42:04.501 --> 42:05.878
-Forty-five. -Fifty.

527
42:05.961 --> 42:07.504
-Forty-five. -Fifty.

528
42:11.467 --> 42:12.926
I give up. Fine, 50 jeon.

529
42:14.094 --> 42:15.346
Thank you.

530
42:15.429 --> 42:17.056
It's so strange.

531
42:17.139 --> 42:19.975
Why does it feel like I always pay you whatever you ask?

532
42:21.143 --> 42:22.019
Tell me about it.

533
42:25.689 --> 42:26.607
Mister.

534
42:27.900 --> 42:30.152
How much do bullets go for?

535
42:32.321 --> 42:33.656
Bullets?

536
42:33.739 --> 42:35.866
Those are hard to come by. How many?

537
42:39.244 --> 42:40.120
Fifty?

538
42:42.206 --> 42:43.082
Ten won.

539
42:43.165 --> 42:44.792
Come on, 30.

540
42:45.918 --> 42:47.378
-Fifteen. -Thirty.

541
42:47.461 --> 42:49.296
-Fifteen. -Thirty.

542
42:49.380 --> 42:52.675
Fine, 20 won. That's it, 20 won.

543
42:52.758 --> 42:54.009
I can't go any higher.

544
42:55.177 --> 42:58.263
Get out of the way. Welcome. Welcome!

545
42:59.515 --> 43:01.100
Twenty won…

546
43:01.183 --> 43:03.310
The going rate must be around 40 won then.

547
43:06.605 --> 43:08.607
Are you saying it's not one of them?

548
43:09.400 --> 43:10.401
Right.

549
43:10.484 --> 43:14.738
But I've never heard of a pickpocket who can speak English.

550
43:14.822 --> 43:18.575
Most of them can't even read their own letters.

551
43:20.994 --> 43:22.705
Then we'll look again.

552
43:22.788 --> 43:26.041
Once we get her, we'll take her to Jongno Police Station and notify the residence.

553
43:27.126 --> 43:28.335
Don't take her to the police.

554
43:29.670 --> 43:30.587
Then what?

555
43:30.671 --> 43:32.798
I want you to contact me directly.

556
43:32.881 --> 43:34.717
The Government-General, not the residence.

557
43:36.343 --> 43:38.053
Will you deal with her yourself?

558
43:38.137 --> 43:39.930
Understood, sir.

559
43:44.309 --> 43:49.064
HANSEONG MEDICINE CLINIC

560
43:53.152 --> 43:55.946
I'll give a prescription for a restorative herbal tonic.

561
43:56.613 --> 43:57.656
Wait here.

562
43:57.740 --> 43:58.615
Here.

563
44:41.366 --> 44:43.827
The gun and bullets for that day,

564
44:44.787 --> 44:46.747
and some rice.

565
44:48.248 --> 44:50.959
The Japs have taken every last grain of rice,

566
44:51.043 --> 44:53.212
so it was very hard to come by.

567
44:53.295 --> 44:54.338
I hope you enjoy it.

568
44:55.172 --> 44:58.801
Thank you. I'm sorry you had to spend such valuable funds.

569
44:59.718 --> 45:02.971
Forgive me. Those bullets were meant for you to use later.

570
45:03.055 --> 45:04.097
No worries.

571
45:06.350 --> 45:07.559
I just can't stand

572
45:07.643 --> 45:10.354
the thought of that Sato bastard eating this precious rice.

573
45:10.437 --> 45:12.105
I want to soak it in poison.

574
45:12.189 --> 45:13.190
We can't use poison.

575
45:16.401 --> 45:19.446
The police will inspect the food before dinner.

576
45:19.530 --> 45:22.241
I know. That's why I brought the gun.

577
45:22.950 --> 45:26.245
Thank you. I'll make sure I succeed.

578
45:27.621 --> 45:31.416
I deliberately approached and married an American who knew nothing in Shanghai

579
45:31.500 --> 45:34.336
and came to Gyeongseong to assassinate Sato.

580
45:34.419 --> 45:38.757
We've been apart for three months. As I've been moody due to the pregnancy,

581
45:38.841 --> 45:41.218
my husband had no idea the pregnancy was fake.

582
45:41.301 --> 45:43.178
You've changed your identity twice.

583
45:43.262 --> 45:44.847
So they'll never trace the link

584
45:44.930 --> 45:47.516
between So-ran and the Gugukdan after the operation.

585
45:47.599 --> 45:51.603
I'll keep an eye on the situation from within the Government-General.

586
45:58.443 --> 46:00.028
During dinner that night…

587
46:01.321 --> 46:02.447
Here's the cake.

588
46:03.574 --> 46:04.491
A cake?

589
46:04.575 --> 46:06.577
My wife makes excellent cakes.

590
46:07.619 --> 46:09.288
By the way, sir.

591
46:17.588 --> 46:18.463
Hands off.

592
46:32.936 --> 46:34.062
What the hell is this?

593
46:38.609 --> 46:40.652
Do you remember Gyeam-ri?

594
46:42.237 --> 46:43.113
Gyeam-ri?

595
46:43.196 --> 46:44.448
April 1919!

596
46:45.532 --> 46:50.078
It's where you shot my daughter and burned 23 other Joseon people alive.

597
46:53.081 --> 46:55.208
Pay for it with your life.

598
47:14.853 --> 47:16.104
Listen, So-ran.

599
47:16.188 --> 47:18.857
I'll wait in the car nearby that day.

600
47:18.941 --> 47:22.361
No. Security will be tight, so we won't be able to get away.

601
47:23.111 --> 47:23.987
Even so…

602
47:24.988 --> 47:26.782
Suzuki, won't you have a gun that day?

603
47:26.865 --> 47:28.367
Don't call me that.

604
47:28.450 --> 47:30.369
Have you already forgotten my Joseon name?

605
47:30.452 --> 47:32.162
Suzuki has to stay.

606
47:32.245 --> 47:33.830
The Gugukdan needs Interpreter Suzuki

607
47:33.914 --> 47:37.417
who can provide us with information from within the Government-General.

608
47:38.293 --> 47:39.628
Besides, Suzuki is the one

609
47:39.711 --> 47:42.923
who's been anonymously reporting our activities and achievements

610
47:43.006 --> 47:44.049
to the newspaper.

611
47:44.132 --> 47:47.928
Thanks to him, those short articles tucked into the corners of the newspaper

612
47:48.011 --> 47:50.931
have been giving the Joseon people a breath of air and hope.

613
47:53.600 --> 47:57.312
I know living as a spy for so many years has been difficult for you.

614
47:58.188 --> 47:59.940
Please keep doing what you're doing.

615
48:02.067 --> 48:03.193
Of course.

616
48:04.820 --> 48:08.323
It took 13 years to track him down

617
48:09.700 --> 48:11.243
and finally get this chance.

618
48:12.869 --> 48:16.373
Once I kill him, there's nothing left for me to live for.

619
48:18.625 --> 48:20.252
So I have to succeed,

620
48:20.836 --> 48:22.796
and I'll gladly die alone.

621
48:22.879 --> 48:26.216
All of you, please welcome Joseon's independence with joy.

622
48:27.926 --> 48:29.469
Even if I fail,

623
48:30.804 --> 48:32.305
I'll be the only one who dies.

624
48:44.735 --> 48:48.447
THREE YEARS AGO, SHANGHAI

625
48:59.958 --> 49:01.752
Why are you looking for the Gugukdan?

626
49:03.336 --> 49:04.254
Don't move.

627
49:04.838 --> 49:05.672
Or I'll shoot.

628
49:12.012 --> 49:14.639
The Joseon people at the sugarcane farm in my hometown, Hawaii,

629
49:14.723 --> 49:17.642
collected 926 dollars for the independence of our country.

630
49:21.855 --> 49:23.523
I'm here to deliver this money.

631
50:07.943 --> 50:09.111
Yes?

632
50:22.666 --> 50:23.875
"Heewon."

633
50:23.959 --> 50:27.087
"Hee" means joy, and "won" is garden. So it's "Garden of Joy."

634
50:32.342 --> 50:36.138
The former owner, a British reporter, left this foundation stone in place

635
50:36.221 --> 50:38.181
when he tore down the hanok and built this house.

636
50:41.685 --> 50:43.145
HEEWON

637
50:43.228 --> 50:44.521
Garden of Joy.

638
50:47.315 --> 50:48.775
When I saw the name…

639
50:54.239 --> 50:56.575
I wished I could spend…

640
50:59.035 --> 51:00.036
many years happily…

641
51:05.250 --> 51:07.127
here with you.

642
51:16.178 --> 51:17.846
You will succeed today.

643
51:23.268 --> 51:24.853
I have a favor to ask.

644
51:28.148 --> 51:30.233
Please make a hanbok for me.

645
51:32.861 --> 51:35.238
Lay me to rest in it when I'm gone.

646
51:37.324 --> 51:39.868
I lost the clothes I'd brought for that.

647
51:39.951 --> 51:41.536
I can't stop thinking about it.

648
51:41.620 --> 51:43.205
So please do it for me.

649
53:35.608 --> 53:37.277
What are you doing?

650
53:41.781 --> 53:43.742
Please show some basic respect.

651
53:46.703 --> 53:47.579
Everybody out.

652
53:49.039 --> 53:49.998
Continue outside.

653
53:50.623 --> 53:51.458
Yes, sir.

654
54:22.322 --> 54:25.033
Welcome, Inspector General.

655
54:25.116 --> 54:26.076
Mr. Suzuki.

656
54:26.159 --> 54:27.869
-Good to see you. -Good evening.

657
54:33.583 --> 54:34.417
Hello.

658
54:39.464 --> 54:41.174
My son came with me.

659
54:41.925 --> 54:43.343
I hope you don't mind.

660
54:43.426 --> 54:45.845
Not at all. He's more than welcome.

661
54:54.896 --> 54:56.398
Let me pour you a drink.

662
54:56.481 --> 54:57.399
Thanks.

663
55:00.610 --> 55:01.611
You too, Mr. Suzuki.

664
55:02.278 --> 55:03.279
Thank you.

665
55:05.657 --> 55:06.574
You too, Mr. Sato.

666
55:07.742 --> 55:09.494
-You don't have to stand-- -No, sir.

667
55:09.577 --> 55:11.162
And please, call me Hideo.

668
55:11.913 --> 55:12.956
Would that be all right?

669
55:13.039 --> 55:13.873
Yes.

670
55:22.090 --> 55:27.345
I know it's rude to bring a gun here. I hope you'll kindly forgive me.

671
55:27.971 --> 55:30.056
Force of habit. For my father's protection.

672
55:36.563 --> 55:37.647
I don't mind at all.

673
55:40.316 --> 55:42.068
A son like him must make you proud.

674
55:42.986 --> 55:46.197
I hope our baby grows up to be like you, Hideo.

675
55:48.491 --> 55:49.784
I certainly hope so.

676
55:50.577 --> 55:51.536
Well, then.

677
55:53.121 --> 55:53.955
Cheers.

678
55:54.038 --> 55:55.540
-Cheers. -Cheers.

679
56:05.884 --> 56:07.635
I hope you'll enjoy the food.

680
56:08.428 --> 56:10.889
It looks absolutely sumptuous.

681
56:10.972 --> 56:14.017
Thank you for preparing such a nice meal tonight.

682
56:14.767 --> 56:16.644
My wife doesn't speak Japanese well.

683
56:16.728 --> 56:18.104
Mr. Inspector General said--

684
56:18.897 --> 56:19.731
That's right.

685
56:20.565 --> 56:22.442
I completely forgot.

686
56:23.276 --> 56:24.903
Let's switch to the Joseon language then.

687
56:26.529 --> 56:29.324
Everything looks absolutely incredible.

688
56:32.368 --> 56:33.286
Thank you.

689
56:34.787 --> 56:36.873
Let me serve you some soup.

690
56:36.956 --> 56:39.000
I should have skipped lunch today.

691
56:39.083 --> 56:40.627
I skipped it.

692
56:41.211 --> 56:42.128
You did? Good.

693
56:44.547 --> 56:47.133
How many dishes did you make today?

694
56:54.516 --> 56:55.350
Six.

695
56:56.351 --> 56:57.185
Six dishes.

696
56:59.020 --> 57:00.522
I made six dishes.

697
57:02.398 --> 57:04.526
She even baked a cake for dessert.

698
57:04.609 --> 57:05.485
Even a cake?

699
57:08.029 --> 57:10.323
For some reason, your wife seems like a Joseon person.

700
57:18.331 --> 57:21.459
But the way she counted on her fingers tells me she really is Chinese.

701
57:27.340 --> 57:30.593
I learned how to count with my fingers the Chinese way

702
57:30.677 --> 57:32.053
while I was in Shanghai.

703
57:33.596 --> 57:34.597
Six.

704
57:35.265 --> 57:36.933
This is how the Chinese do it.

705
57:37.016 --> 57:38.768
Joseon does it this way.

706
57:38.851 --> 57:40.687
And Japan does it this way.

707
57:40.770 --> 57:42.063
That's right.

708
57:43.147 --> 57:44.566
Did you know the difference?

709
57:45.233 --> 57:47.569
Yes, I learned it at the Army Academy.

710
57:54.409 --> 57:57.078
I ordered a cake from Itsukoshi Department Store.

711
57:57.745 --> 58:00.623
I didn't know your wife had baked a cake,

712
58:00.707 --> 58:02.125
so I made a mistake.

713
58:02.208 --> 58:03.793
Not at all. It's thoughtful of you.

714
58:03.876 --> 58:05.211
Thank you.

715
58:05.920 --> 58:07.088
I'll…

716
58:07.171 --> 58:09.716
I'll get the door. Please continue, gentlemen.

717
58:09.799 --> 58:10.758
Would you?

718
58:16.764 --> 58:17.974
-All right. -Yes.

719
58:25.231 --> 58:26.274
Where's the cake…?

720
58:26.357 --> 58:29.402
She says she's a live-in maid here.

721
58:29.485 --> 58:30.570
Is that true?

722
58:31.863 --> 58:34.032
He doesn't speak this language.

723
58:34.115 --> 58:36.534
I'll give the bullets back. Just give me 60 won.

724
58:37.952 --> 58:39.412
So it's you. The pickpocket.

725
58:39.495 --> 58:41.998
If you stall now, he'll catch on.

726
58:42.081 --> 58:43.166
You'll pay me, right?

727
58:45.793 --> 58:46.961
Ma'am?

728
58:47.545 --> 58:49.881
Is she your live-in maid?

729
58:52.842 --> 58:53.843
Come in.

730
58:55.261 --> 58:56.888
I'm going in, then.

731
59:03.811 --> 59:06.731
The taxi driver at Gyeongseong Station remembered you right away.

732
59:07.523 --> 59:11.861
He said a lady who looked great in a qipao got off at a very nice house.

733
59:13.279 --> 59:15.448
This house is so amazing.

734
59:16.407 --> 59:17.367
Whatever you're up to--

735
59:17.450 --> 59:20.870
If you lock me up or threaten me, I'll scream and make a scene.

736
59:21.704 --> 59:23.956
Then they'll all hear it.

737
59:24.582 --> 59:25.416
Right?

738
59:27.043 --> 59:29.462
The Government-General's number two is here.

739
59:33.633 --> 59:35.343
Give me 60 won,

740
59:35.426 --> 59:36.678
and I'll leave quietly.

741
59:46.646 --> 59:48.564
Sixty won, not six.

742
59:49.148 --> 59:50.316
That's all I have now.

743
59:50.400 --> 59:52.276
Wait here quietly, and I'll get the rest later.

744
59:54.696 --> 59:55.697
All right.

745
59:57.198 --> 59:59.158
I'll bring the bullets tomorrow.

746
59:59.242 --> 01:00:01.828
I didn't bring them since there'd be police everywhere.

747
01:00:02.537 --> 01:00:04.163
Stay here until I get back.

748
01:00:04.247 --> 01:00:05.623
Don't try anything stupid.

749
01:00:06.999 --> 01:00:08.000
Stupid?

750
01:00:09.961 --> 01:00:11.212
Don't worry.

751
01:00:11.295 --> 01:00:14.382
I couldn't care less what you'll do with those bullets.

752
01:00:16.801 --> 01:00:19.220
It's not like anyone's going to pay me to tell

753
01:00:19.303 --> 01:00:22.223
the Government-General's number two

754
01:00:22.306 --> 01:00:24.183
that you smuggled bullets in.

755
01:00:25.643 --> 01:00:26.686
I'll be waiting.

756
01:00:29.063 --> 01:00:30.815
You have quite an eye.

757
01:00:31.315 --> 01:00:32.817
Oh, you think so?

758
01:00:44.746 --> 01:00:46.998
You took so long, I was about to send him after you.

759
01:00:47.081 --> 01:00:48.708
Is there a problem with the cake?

760
01:00:49.542 --> 01:00:52.628
No, it wasn't the cake. It was our live-in maid.

761
01:00:55.715 --> 01:00:57.467
I sent her on an errand earlier.

762
01:00:57.550 --> 01:00:59.802
I scolded her for staying out late playing around.

763
01:01:01.262 --> 01:01:02.388
Again?

764
01:01:03.890 --> 01:01:05.183
The food is delicious.

765
01:01:05.975 --> 01:01:06.809
Thank you.

766
01:01:15.902 --> 01:01:19.113
I said 60 so I could come down to 50, but she didn't even haggle.

767
01:01:20.698 --> 01:01:22.074
I should've started at 100.

768
01:01:59.862 --> 01:02:01.322
An American passport?

769
01:02:11.958 --> 01:02:13.042
It's real.

770
01:02:26.597 --> 01:02:27.807
By the way, sir,

771
01:02:28.391 --> 01:02:30.560
I always think about how I can be of service

772
01:02:30.643 --> 01:02:32.353
to the Government-General.

773
01:02:32.436 --> 01:02:33.980
So I wanted to discuss--

774
01:02:34.063 --> 01:02:35.565
-What is it? -Yes.

775
01:02:39.443 --> 01:02:41.946
I suppose this is a rather sensitive issue.

776
01:02:43.823 --> 01:02:48.035
So I was wondering if the others could give us a moment alone.

777
01:02:49.370 --> 01:02:51.914
Is it something these two shouldn't hear?

778
01:02:53.249 --> 01:02:54.584
If you don't mind.

779
01:02:55.918 --> 01:02:56.919
Very well.

780
01:02:57.837 --> 01:02:59.338
Give us the room. You too.

781
01:02:59.422 --> 01:03:00.631
Sure.

782
01:03:09.765 --> 01:03:11.267
Can you step out for a moment?

783
01:03:12.184 --> 01:03:14.186
All right. Then…

784
01:03:15.479 --> 01:03:16.772
I'll go get the cake.

785
01:03:41.547 --> 01:03:43.591
Excuse me, where's the bathroom?

786
01:03:43.674 --> 01:03:45.051
Right this way.

787
01:03:46.719 --> 01:03:48.679
I'll go check on the kitchen.

788
01:03:48.763 --> 01:03:49.597
All right.

789
01:04:01.859 --> 01:04:04.153
Keep Hideo distracted in the living room.

790
01:04:25.883 --> 01:04:26.717
I'm sorry.

791
01:04:44.235 --> 01:04:45.236
Hello.

792
01:04:46.862 --> 01:04:48.489
I didn't expect to see you here.

793
01:04:52.702 --> 01:04:56.205
Gyeongseong really is a small place.

794
01:04:57.665 --> 01:04:58.666
Excuse me?

795
01:05:00.710 --> 01:05:03.170
I was impressed by your pickpocketing skills.

796
01:05:06.382 --> 01:05:07.758
I'm not sure what you mean.

797
01:05:08.968 --> 01:05:11.220
It's a compliment. I was genuinely impressed.

798
01:05:11.804 --> 01:05:13.222
I was quite hopeless myself.

799
01:05:14.473 --> 01:05:16.392
Would you mind telling me your secret?

800
01:05:16.475 --> 01:05:18.352
It might come in handy someday.

801
01:05:20.187 --> 01:05:21.939
I'm afraid I don't understand.

802
01:05:23.065 --> 01:05:26.694
I work here as a live-in maid.

803
01:05:27.737 --> 01:05:28.571
I see.

804
01:05:29.613 --> 01:05:32.825
Come to think of it, she said she was from mainland Japan.

805
01:05:34.535 --> 01:05:37.204
I must have mistaken you for someone else.

806
01:05:38.164 --> 01:05:39.707
All right, then.

807
01:05:41.667 --> 01:05:43.544
What did you steal upstairs just now?

808
01:05:47.131 --> 01:05:50.259
Why do you keep accusing me of…

809
01:05:51.093 --> 01:05:51.927
stealing?

810
01:05:52.803 --> 01:05:54.138
If you keep suspecting me,

811
01:05:54.221 --> 01:05:57.308
I'll take off my clothes and prove my innocence.

812
01:05:58.142 --> 01:05:59.101
No need.

813
01:05:59.894 --> 01:06:01.062
I apologize.

814
01:06:05.941 --> 01:06:07.234
That reminds me.

815
01:06:07.318 --> 01:06:09.278
Did you see the princess's photo?

816
01:06:12.198 --> 01:06:13.115
My wallet.

817
01:06:14.617 --> 01:06:15.493
I'd like it back.

818
01:06:16.869 --> 01:06:18.579
I don't know what you're talking--

819
01:06:18.662 --> 01:06:19.997
Enough with the act.

820
01:06:27.630 --> 01:06:30.132
Just return my wallet, and we can end this quietly.

821
01:06:31.634 --> 01:06:33.552
Making a scene won't do either of us any good.

822
01:06:37.473 --> 01:06:38.474
Who is it?

823
01:06:40.684 --> 01:06:41.852
And you are…

824
01:06:43.729 --> 01:06:45.189
Are you the live-in maid?

825
01:06:46.107 --> 01:06:48.150
Yes, I'm the maid.

826
01:06:49.902 --> 01:06:51.737
I was on my way out on an errand.

827
01:06:58.494 --> 01:06:59.370
You startled me.

828
01:07:01.330 --> 01:07:02.289
How can I help you?

829
01:07:03.207 --> 01:07:06.919
Are you expecting a cake from Itsukoshi Department Store?

830
01:07:24.854 --> 01:07:27.398
So, what exactly is this sensitive issue?

831
01:07:28.607 --> 01:07:29.525
Right.

832
01:07:32.403 --> 01:07:34.238
Yesterday, President Hoover--

833
01:07:34.321 --> 01:07:35.281
One moment.

834
01:07:35.364 --> 01:07:37.199
Let me use the bathroom first.

835
01:07:37.283 --> 01:07:38.701
I've had too much to drink.

836
01:07:41.954 --> 01:07:43.038
That's right.

837
01:07:44.540 --> 01:07:46.417
The inspector general ordered it.

838
01:07:46.500 --> 01:07:47.710
Yes, sir.

839
01:07:49.712 --> 01:07:52.089
Aren't you going to get the cake?

840
01:07:52.965 --> 01:07:53.799
Sure.

841
01:07:54.758 --> 01:07:55.593
Give it to me.

842
01:07:58.095 --> 01:07:59.221
The cake is here.

843
01:08:29.293 --> 01:08:30.586
The cake is…

844
01:08:45.684 --> 01:08:46.977
Where's the bathroom?

845
01:08:47.061 --> 01:08:48.354
It's that way.

846
01:09:05.579 --> 01:09:07.331
-Hideo. -Yes.

847
01:09:15.673 --> 01:09:18.217
It's the second door down the hall.

848
01:09:28.644 --> 01:09:31.272
Bring the cake when I call for you.

849
01:09:34.400 --> 01:09:37.027
I wonder if Mr. Yoo has a cigarette.

850
01:09:43.450 --> 01:09:44.535
Come in.

851
01:10:04.847 --> 01:10:06.598
She's the pickpocket who stole the bullets?

852
01:10:07.599 --> 01:10:08.434
Yes.

853
01:10:08.517 --> 01:10:12.021
But once I kill Sato, it won't matter what she says.

854
01:10:12.730 --> 01:10:14.398
I'll shoot Sato when he walks in.

855
01:10:14.481 --> 01:10:16.442
Philip will be my hostage.

856
01:10:25.617 --> 01:10:29.038
Excuse me, I need to head out soon.

857
01:10:29.121 --> 01:10:31.749
You can put the cake over there…

858
01:10:33.250 --> 01:10:34.543
Take me to the bathroom.

859
01:10:36.462 --> 01:10:38.380
Make a sound, and you'll die first.

860
01:10:45.596 --> 01:10:47.639
I'll leave the rest to you.

861
01:10:47.723 --> 01:10:48.807
Thank you for everything.

862
01:11:39.608 --> 01:11:42.194
Wait. We're not done talking.

863
01:11:50.244 --> 01:11:51.245
What?

864
01:13:03.066 --> 01:13:05.694
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

865
01:13:07.988 --> 01:13:08.822
Who are you really?

866
01:13:12.242 --> 01:13:14.745
Where did he run off to? Say it!

867
01:13:14.828 --> 01:13:16.371
Think carefully.

868
01:13:16.455 --> 01:13:19.041
Give me what's in my wallet, and I'll let this all go.

869
01:13:19.124 --> 01:13:21.210
I don't trust Josenjing.

870
01:13:21.293 --> 01:13:23.462
If you get caught, do you think I'll be safe?

871
01:13:24.213 --> 01:13:25.672
They're looking for her.

872
01:13:25.756 --> 01:13:28.217
For 13 years, I didn't know if he was alive.

873
01:13:28.300 --> 01:13:29.343
Keum Seo-hee!

874
01:13:29.426 --> 01:13:31.720
Could this be some kind of fate?

875
01:13:32.679 --> 01:13:35.349
There's no way we'll see each other again.

876
01:13:36.225 --> 01:13:37.476
Do you want to get rid of her?

877
01:13:44.942 --> 01:13:46.944
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
